{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01112",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.34,
      "end_seconds": 6.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "doctor, if you're free, we can start. I've got the numbers noted down"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.29,
      "end_seconds": 11.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "thank you good morning, tell me what's been going on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.88,
      "end_seconds": 19.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "Um, so... a grinding sound when I move. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.61,
      "end_seconds": 21.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.38,
      "end_seconds": 25.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "It's been six months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.88,
      "end_seconds": 29.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Understood. Alright, how troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.73,
      "end_seconds": 34.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "A eight out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.74,
      "end_seconds": 36.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "I see, go ahead"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.56,
      "end_seconds": 48.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.14,
      "text": "oh, and swelling in the right knee. That's been about the same, three weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.28,
      "end_seconds": 52.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "how troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.9,
      "end_seconds": 66.67,
      "duration_seconds": 13.77,
      "text": "About a eight out of ten. There's pain in both knees as well. With pain in both knees, it sort of comes and goes. I notice it more with squatting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 85.28,
      "end_seconds": 93.98,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Okay, so so the vitals from earlier. Oxygen saturation is 97 percent, pressure 114 over 77, pulse 82, temp 36.7 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.09,
      "end_seconds": 95.79,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.19,
      "end_seconds": 102.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.27,
      "end_seconds": 105.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.91,
      "end_seconds": 127.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "there's mild swelling on the right knee, and a grating feel when I bend it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.59,
      "end_seconds": 137.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Any fall, locking of the knee or back pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.33,
      "end_seconds": 145.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.83,
      "text": "No fall, locking of the knee or back pain, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.65,
      "end_seconds": 151.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "a few quick ones: fever or redness over the knee?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.01,
      "end_seconds": 157.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "No, no fever or redness over the knee."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.57,
      "end_seconds": 164.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "alright, have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.25,
      "end_seconds": 167.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.24,
      "end_seconds": 173.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.75,
      "end_seconds": 176.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.98,
      "end_seconds": 180.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.53,
      "end_seconds": 183.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Diabetes, for about a year"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.63,
      "end_seconds": 193.46,
      "duration_seconds": 8.83,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes is known to us, good to have that clear. Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.69,
      "end_seconds": 198.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Yes, naproxen, it gives me a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.93,
      "end_seconds": 202.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.89,
      "end_seconds": 214.28,
      "duration_seconds": 11.39,
      "text": "Yes, I had a mole taken off my arm, a few years ago. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.14,
      "end_seconds": 218.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.81,
      "end_seconds": 231.04,
      "duration_seconds": 11.23,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother. I swim twice a week. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.72,
      "end_seconds": 234.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.79,
      "end_seconds": 247.47,
      "duration_seconds": 11.68,
      "text": "Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar. I do miss it now and then, to be fair. Volini gel, twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.28,
      "end_seconds": 252.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Alright, how long have you taken that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.9,
      "end_seconds": 255.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "About about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.13,
      "end_seconds": 256.83,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.06,
      "end_seconds": 284.05,
      "duration_seconds": 12.99,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, the most likely explanation is osteoarthritis of the knees. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.81,
      "end_seconds": 286.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.1,
      "end_seconds": 296.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now osteoarthritis of the knees is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.57,
      "end_seconds": 337.36,
      "duration_seconds": 24.79,
      "text": "I'm sending you for blood tests because of joint pain. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'm going to order an X-ray of both knees, for knee pain. You'll be taking paracetamol, 650 milligrams, three times a day, for two weeks. You take it by mouth. That should help with knee pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.38,
      "end_seconds": 341.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Is that safe with my other medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.42,
      "end_seconds": 368.92,
      "duration_seconds": 22.5,
      "text": "Losing even a few kilos takes a lot of load off the knees, and I'd like you to do the strengthening exercises. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.74,
      "end_seconds": 372.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Yes, will do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.44,
      "end_seconds": 383.88,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "I'll want another look in six weeks. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.55,
      "end_seconds": 391.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 394.95,
      "end_seconds": 396.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}